From: ROG5 Linux bring-up <rog5@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: flush all ports on normal gen1 capture streamoff

Chromium stops CAPTURE before OUTPUT when closing a stateful decoder.
The gen1 path treats this like a resolution change and sends FLUSH_OUTPUT
while compressed input is still pending. On SM8350 with vpu20_4v.mbn this
is followed by an unanswered flush and unresponsive firmware.

Follow Venus vdec_stop_capture(): use FLUSH_ALL for ordinary streamoff,
reserving FLUSH_OUTPUT for dynamic resolution change, where input is
paused. A closing instance also needs FLUSH_ALL even if DRC is pending.
Keep the existing flush completion wait before STOP/RELEASE_RESOURCES.
OUTPUT2 is not a substitute: stock and Venus use FLUSH_OUTPUT for DRC
with secondary display output too.

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
@@ -477,10 +477,12 @@
 
 	if (inst->domain == DECODER) {
 		if (inst->state == IRIS_INST_STREAMING) {
-			if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(plane))
+			/* Output-only flush is for a paused resolution change. */
+			if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_CAPTURE(plane) &&
+			    (inst->sub_state & IRIS_INST_SUB_DRC) && !inst->closing)
+				flush_type = HFI_FLUSH_OUTPUT;
+			else
 				flush_type = HFI_FLUSH_ALL;
-			else if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_CAPTURE(plane))
-				flush_type = HFI_FLUSH_OUTPUT;
 
 			reinit_completion(&inst->flush_completion);
 
